From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] OverlayRendererGLES: draw nothing for an empty bitmap

A palette overlay of width or height 0 went on to FindVisibleBox, which
reports a 1x1 box for it, and ConvertIndices then read the first pixel of an
empty pixel vector. The texture constructor now returns before creating a
texture when the bitmap has no pixels, and Render draws nothing for an overlay
without a texture (texture 0 would sample opaque black).

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/OverlayRendererGLES.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/OverlayRendererGLES.cpp
index 5950d41327..62ee1621f8 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/OverlayRendererGLES.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/OverlayRendererGLES.cpp
@@ -161,6 +161,10 @@ COverlayTextureGLES::COverlayTextureGLES(const CDVDOverlayImage& o, CRect& rSour
 {
   m_isHDROverlay = o.m_isHDROverlay;
 
+  // an empty bitmap has no pixel to read; it stays without a texture and draws nothing
+  if (o.width <= 0 || o.height <= 0)
+    return;
+
   glGenTextures(1, &m_texture);
   glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, m_texture);
 
@@ -488,6 +492,9 @@ COverlayTextureGLES::~COverlayTextureGLES()
 
 void COverlayTextureGLES::Render(SRenderState& state)
 {
+  if (m_texture == 0)
+    return;
+
   glEnable(GL_BLEND);
 
   glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, m_texture);
